WEBVTT

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:13.233
The events of Romeo and Juliet take place in Verona, Italy.  The two most influential families in that city, the Montagues and the Capulets, have been at war with each other for a

00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:20.015
long time.  At the beginning of the play, the servants of the Montagues and Capulets get into a fight with each other.

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:27.780
Benvolio, a member of the Montague family, tries to stop the fight, but one of the Capulets, Tybalt, starts fighting him.

00:00:28.781 --> 00:00:37.196
Eventually, the prince arrives and breaks up the fight.  He tells the Montagues and Capulets, the heads of the families, that he will execute them if it happens again.

00:00:39.193 --> 00:00:44.846
Afterwards, the Montagues and Lady Montagues ask Benvolio where their son Romeo was during the fight.

00:00:45.094 --> 00:00:49.225
Benvolio says that Romeo is not himself, but he will find out why.

00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:52.864
Romeo confesses to Benvolio that he is suffering from love.

00:00:52.964 --> 00:01:00.994
He is in love with a girl named Rosalina, who does not reciprocate his love.  Benvolio promises to help Romeo forget her.  Count

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:05.245
Paris says he wants to marry the Capulet's only daughter, Juliet.

00:01:05.345 --> 00:01:13.611
Capulet asks Paris to wait a few years, as Juliet is only 13, but allows him to try to win her favor.  He invites Paris to a

00:01:13.643 --> 00:01:21.307
celebratory feast that evening.  The Capulet servant walks around the city, trying to invite people from the list to the banquet.

00:01:21.407 --> 00:01:29.877
The problem is that the servant can't read. He stops Benvolio and Romeo and asks them for help.  Romeo sees Rosaline's name on the list, and Benvolio

00:01:29.907 --> 00:01:38.887
says they should sneak into the party so Romeo can compare Rosaline to other girls and fall out of love with her.  Romeo agrees to go, but only to see

00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:47.402
Rosaline.  Lady Capulet, Juliet, and her nurse discuss Paris's intention to marry Juliet.  Lady Capulet and the nurse

00:01:47.435 --> 00:01:51.288
praise him in every way .  Juliet agrees to meet him.

00:01:52.971 --> 00:02:02.030
Romeo, Benvolio, and Mercutio sneak into the banquet in masks.  At the party, Romeo sees Juliet and completely forgets about Rosaline.

00:02:02.144 --> 00:02:10.236
He is in love. Capulet's nephew, Tybalt, recognizes Romeo's voice and is furious that he has sneaked inside.

00:02:10.872 --> 00:02:19.511
Capulet orders Tybalt to calm down , as he does not want a fight at his feast.  Romeo finds Juliet, takes her hand and

00:02:19.542 --> 00:02:28.178
persuades her to let him kiss him. All this time they talk to each other in verse.  After this meeting, each of them tries to find out who the other is.

00:02:28.278 --> 00:02:36.842
They are upset to learn that they belong to feuding families, but both decide that they are too much in love to back down.  After

00:02:36.872 --> 00:02:41.518
the party, Romeo leaves his friends and climbs over the garden wall to see Juliet.

00:02:41.618 --> 00:02:49.876
He sees her on the balcony, where she is talking to herself.  Before she realizes that Romeo is eavesdropping, Juliet confesses that she loves him.  Romeo

00:02:49.913 --> 00:02:58.992
comes out of hiding and says he loves her too. Romeo asks his confessor, Brother Lorenzo, to perform the marriage ceremony.

00:02:59.741 --> 00:03:07.948
Friar Lorenzo is concerned about how quickly Romeo has switched from Rosaline to Juliet, but agrees because he believes it will bring peace to the warring

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:16.387
families.  Mercutio and Benvolio tell Romeo that Tybalt wants to challenge him to a duel.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:24.538
Juliet's nurse arrives, wanting to talk to Romeo alone.  Romeo asks her to tell Juliet to come to Lorenzo's in the afternoon for the

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:32.566
wedding.  Juliet meets Romeo and the monk in his cell, and he marries them.

00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:35.753
Tybalt later finds Romeo and tries to start a fight.

00:03:35.853 --> 00:03:39.340
Romeo doesn't want to fight Tybalt because he is Juliet's cousin.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:48.301
Mercutio steps in to fight Tybalt in his place.  Romeo tries to separate them, but Tybalt stabs Mercutio out of

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:56.889
Romeo's hand with his sword and flees. Mercutio dies, cursing both families.  Romeo is furious, and when Tybalt returns

00:03:56.889 --> 00:04:03.669
, Romeo kills him and then flees. The prince arrives, and Benvolio tells him what happened.

00:04:03.922 --> 00:04:12.645
The Prince announces that Romeo is banished from Verona.  Juliet is eagerly awaiting her wedding night with Romeo when

00:04:12.678 --> 00:04:15.929
the nurse arrives and announces that Romeo has killed Tybalt and is banished.

00:04:16.029 --> 00:04:20.577
At first, Juliet is angry with Romeo, but then decides that she is on his side.

00:04:20.677 --> 00:04:29.780
Juliet sends a nurse to tell Romeo to spend the night with her .  Friar Lorenzo tells Romeo the news of his banishment, and he wants to commit

00:04:29.812 --> 00:04:38.465
suicide.    The nurse arrives and orders Romeo to go to Juliet's that night.    The monk tells Romeo to go to Mantua the next morning and

00:04:38.496 --> 00:04:48.355
wait for news from him.  Capulet decides that he will marry Juliet to Paris in just 3 days.  After a

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:56.968
night together, Romeo and Juliet playfully argue about whether it is dawn yet, until they are forced to admit it, and Romeo leaves.  Lady Capulet tells

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:05.085
Juliet that she must marry Paris.  Juliet refuses, but Capulet himself enters and says he will disown her if she

00:05:05.116 --> 00:05:13.891
disobeys. disobeys. Juliet goes to her brother Lorenzo and says that she will kill herself if he does not help her get out of her predicament.

00:05:13.891 --> 00:05:21.959
predicament. He gives her a vial of potion and tells her to agree to the marriage, then drink it the night before the wedding.  For 42

00:05:21.994 --> 00:05:26.871
hours, she will appear dead, and her family will place her in the family crypt.

00:05:27.592 --> 00:05:34.048
Friar Lorenzo will write to Romeo about everything, and together they will wait for her to wake up so they can take her to Mantua.

00:05:34.577 --> 00:05:43.506
Juliet agrees. agrees. Juliet goes to her father and tells him that Brother Lorenzo taught her to be obedient.  Capulet is

00:05:43.536 --> 00:05:51.724
so happy about this change that he postpones the wedding until the next day.  That night, Juliet hesitates to take

00:05:51.756 --> 00:05:56.775
the potion, thinking about how scary it would be to wake up in a crypt, but decides to drink it anyway.

00:05:59.007 --> 00:06:07.166
The next day, the Capulets find Juliet dead in bed .  Paris and brother Lorenzo arrive for the wedding.  The Capulets

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:15.482
, Lady Capulets, the Nurse, and Paris mourn their loss, but Friar Lorenzo assures them that Juliet is in a better world.  They prepare

00:06:15.514 --> 00:06:23.899
to carry Juliet to her tomb.  In Mantua, Romeo wakes up expecting good news.  His servant Balthazar arrives and

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:32.798
announces that Juliet has died. Romeo decides to commit suicide and lie down next to Juliet.  He goes to a pharmacist who makes and sells

00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:41.429
medicine and bribes him to sell poison, which is a capital offense.  A priest named Brother Giovanni informs Brother

00:06:41.459 --> 00:06:45.412
Lorenzo that he was unable to deliver the news of Juliet's feigned death to Romeo.

00:06:45.512 --> 00:06:50.689
Brother Giovanni says he was quarantined because the authorities decided he might have contracted the plague.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:58.689
Friar Lorenzo sends him to get a crowbar and says that Juliet will wake up in 3 hours and will be angry with him for not warning Romeo.

00:07:00.368 --> 00:07:08.590
Paris arrives at the crypt with his page and orders him to lie down under the trees and whistle if anyone approaches.  He brings flowers to

00:07:08.622 --> 00:07:13.533
Juliet's grave.  The page whistles because Romeo is approaching, and Paris hides.

00:07:14.192 --> 00:07:21.657
Romeo arrives.  He orders Balthazar to leave, but he hides and remains nearby.  Romeo opens the crypt.

00:07:22.928 --> 00:07:31.132
Paris tries to arrest Romeo. Romeo says he has come to commit suicide and does not want to harm Paris, but he insists on being arrested, and they

00:07:31.164 --> 00:07:39.601
begin to fight.  The page runs away to call the guard.  Romeo kills Paris.  Paris asks to be laid next to Juliet, Romeo

00:07:39.632 --> 00:07:48.856
agrees and drags his body to the crypt.  Romeo kisses Juliet, drinks the poison, kisses her again, and dies, lying on

00:07:48.894 --> 00:07:56.940
Juliet's chest. Friar Lorenzo arrives at the cemetery, learns from Balthazar that Romeo is there, and enters the

00:07:56.973 --> 00:08:05.043
crypt, where he finds Juliet alive.  He explains that the plan didn't work, a higher power prevented it, and that she needs to leave, and he

00:08:05.077 --> 00:08:10.077
will find her a place in the monastery.  He runs away because he thinks the guard is approaching.

00:08:10.203 --> 00:08:19.085
Juliet refuses to go. She sees that Romeo has been poisoned and kisses him, hoping to get some of the poison.  Then she hears someone coming,

00:08:19.119 --> 00:08:23.807
takes Romeo's dagger and stabs it into her chest.

00:08:23.839 --> 00:08:32.993
The head guard arrives and finds the bodies.  He sends the guards to gather everyone nearby and bring in the prince, the Capulets, and the Montagues.  The guards

00:08:33.027 --> 00:08:41.696
bring in Balthazar and the monk Lorenzo. Friar Lorenzo explains everything that happened.  The prince says that the Capulets and

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:49.787
Montagues have already been punished for their enmity, and he himself is punished for tolerating their enmity, because he lost two relatives, Mercutio and Paris.

00:08:51.761 --> 00:09:02.047
The Montagues promise to build a golden statue of Juliet, and the Capulets promise to make the same for Romeo.  To learn

00:09:02.077 --> 00:09:10.240
more about “Romeo and Juliet,” check out SparkNote about “Romeo and Juliet” at sparknotes.com.  For a translation of the entire play in modern

00:09:10.275 --> 00:09:14.470
English, go to No Fear Shakespeare at nfs.sparknotes.com.
